{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Your father and your brothers have come to you.</b> This is an introductory formulation, as if to say: Behold, I have heard that your father and your brothers have come, and the land of Egypt is before you. But the correct interpretation in my eyes is that he says, \"Your father and your brothers have come to you\" — to hear your glory, and upon you they have cast their dependence. See that you do good with them, for the matter is upon you, and your hand is over all."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:22:24.354036445Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}